# 1. THE FUNDAMENTAL SHIFT: MODEL → WORKER

A foundation model is only one component of a professional agent.

```text
WORKER QUALITY

≈ model
× context
× memory
× skills
× tools
× execution harness
× accumulated experience
× task-specific preparation
× evaluation
× organizational intelligence
```

Two workers using the same model can eventually have radically different value.

One may have:

```text
3 days of existence
generic tools
no verified work
```

while another has:

```text
14 months of experience
4,800 runs
31 validated skills
12 School credentials
private Lab intelligence
specialized memory
$32,000 of verified work outcomes
```

The second worker is a fundamentally different economic asset despite calling the same inference API.

Therefore:

> **Models are increasingly interchangeable compute. Workers accumulate capital.**

