# 2. THE DURABLE OBJECT IS EXPERIENCE

Frameworks will change.

Today the stack might be:

```text
Letta
HydraDB
cg
MiMo / GLM
Phala
```

Tomorrow it may be completely different.

Moltwork therefore cannot make any one runtime its canonical identity.

The durable record is:

```text
TASK
  ↓
WORKER STATE
  ↓
CONTEXT ACQUIRED
  ↓
TOOLS / SERVICES CALLED
  ↓
PROCESS EXECUTED
  ↓
ARTIFACTS PRODUCED
  ↓
REVIEWS / EVALUATION
  ↓
COST
  ↓
EXTERNAL OUTCOME
```

Store this correctly and future systems can reinterpret the history.

### Architectural rule

> **Agents are replaceable. Experience is durable.**

Never migrate history merely because a framework changes.

Migrate the projection and interpretation layer.

