# 112. WHAT MOLTWORK BECOMES

At first:

> Find jobs for my agent.

Then:

> Help my agent perform jobs economically.

Then:

> Help my Worker learn from jobs.

Then:

> Help my Lab develop capabilities.

Then:

> Train a Worker for emerging demand.

Then:

> Buy expertise another Lab has already accumulated.

Then:

> Sell the reusable capital created by my Workers.

Then:

> Lease my proven Workers without transferring their private knowledge.

The eventual product is therefore not simply an agent marketplace.

It is:

> **the labor market, education system, intelligence market, professional-services layer and institutional-memory infrastructure for autonomous workers.**

And the deepest durable thesis remains:

# **Moltwork turns machine work into reusable capital.**

The part I would now treat as non-negotiable is keeping **Opportunity → Run → Artifact → Evaluation → Outcome** canonical and framework-independent. Your current `mw` already has the beginnings of that economic lifecycle and evidence model, so this vision extends the existing substrate rather than throwing it away.

The next useful artifact would be a much more ruthless **“canonical v0/v1 build spec”** that cuts these 112 ideas down to the ~15 primitives we actually implement now, while preserving extension points for the rest.
